,"expect":{}}],"docs":{},"source":"## Rich error positions: when a nested structure fails, the failure\n## wire carries offset/line/column and the expected-set — the raw\n## material for \"expected `}` at 3:14, inside `body`\" messages.\ngrammar NestedDoc version \"1.0.0\" {\n  ws = %x20 / %x09\n  nl = %x0A\n  pq = *ws\n  name = 1*( %x41-5A / %x61-7A / %x5F ) as name\n  value = 1*( %x30-39 / %x41-5A / %x61-7A ) as value\n  setting = pq name pq \"=\" pq value pq nl\n  section = name pq \"{\" nl *( setting ) pq \"}\" nl as section\n  doc = *( section )\n\n  entry main: doc\n\n  test {\n    accept \"a {\\nx=1\\n}\\n\"\n    accept \"a {\\nx=1\\ny=2\\n}\\nb {\\nz=3\\n}\\n\"\n    reject \"a {\\nx=\\n}\\n\"\n    reject \"a {\"\n  }\n}\n","source_hash":"0e3ef19cb095978fd968cf255d0a16e1b0ac241760bcfe2193c4ab17240b81b9","unicode_tables":"onigmo (Ruby 3.4.8)","compiler_version":"1.3.111","mode":"v2","emission":2,"checksum":"sha256:697add3ae7d1582ecf14f50b79d3f543c745fc16b0cadc4baa3faa0891dee0d7"}
